{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so I've got an ADK agent (python, a root agent plus two sub-agents for looking up invoices) that runs fine with `adk web` locally. My manager wants it on GCP by end of next week for a 2-week pilot with the finance team. I've never deployed anything there. Should this go on Cloud Run, Agent Engine, or GKE? Walk me through it end to end: which service account it should run as and what roles it needs, how to containerize it, how I confirm the dev UI actually loads after deploy, what to do if the new revision breaks, and how to tear it all down cleanly when the pilot ends so we don't get billed."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "First time putting an agent on Google Cloud. Built with ADK, works on my Mac. Need: pick a hosting option, minimal-permission identity, Dockerfile or whatever's needed, a smoke test in the browser, a rollback plan, and a cleanup script for afterwards. It's a throwaway demo so keep it simple."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "Our ADK agent is already running on Cloud Run and has been for months, but responses got really slow since last Tuesday, sometimes 20+ seconds before the first token. Nothing changed in the deploy as far as I know. The tool calls to BigQuery seem to be where it hangs?? How do I figure out what's going on?", "needs_instead": "Performance troubleshooting of an agent that is already deployed: tracing and logs, latency in tool calls, and BigQuery query tuning. This is not a first-time deployment or hosting choice."}
]}
